's threshold is not, by itself, an adequate basis for disapproval. Idaho's approach is well reasoned and therefore we continue to find that Idaho documented a reasonable approach to evaluating costs and met its obligations under 40 CFR 51.308(f)(2)(i).", "passage_polarity": "positive", "signals": [{"signal_text": "Idahi used a cost-effectiveness threshold that is lower than another State's threshold is not, by itself, an adequate basis for disapproval", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "positive", "rubric_matches": [140, 141, 142], "_snap_kind": "no_match"}], "_snap_kind": "anchor_only"}]}, "raw_text": "{\"unit_id\": \"EPA-R10-OAR-2024-0545-0085\", \"passages\": [{\"passage_text\": \"On that basis, we find that Idaho included adequate information and an explanation of its source selection methodology in its regional haze plan submission and that the information submitted supports a finding that Idaho examined a reasonable set of sources for the second implementation period.\", \"passage_polarity\": \"positive\", \"signals\": [{\"signal_text\": \"we find that Idaho included adequate information and an explanation of its source selection methodology in its regional haze plan submission\", \"signal_type\": \"observation\", \"rubric_matches\": [20, 32, 35]}]}, {\"passage_text\": \"As the EPA stated in the NPRM, the EPA did not establish a cost-effectiveness threshold for the second implementation period. Rather, the EPA's 2019 Guidance clarified that States had the flexibility to decide a reasonable approach to evaluating costs.\", \"passage_polarity\": \"positive\", \"signals\": [{\"signal_text\": \"the EPA did not establish a cost-effectiveness threshold for the second implementation period\", \"signal_type\": \"observation\", \"polarity\": \"positive\", \"rubic_matches\": [139, 192]}, {\"signal_text\": \"the EPA's 2019 Guidance clarified that States had the flexibility to decide a reasonable approach to evaluating costs\", \"signal_type\": \"observation\", \"polarity\": \"positive\", \"rubic_matches\": [1, 15, 21]}]}, {\"passage_text\": \"The fact that Idaho used a cost-effectiveness threshold that is lower than another State's threshold is not, by itself, an adequate basis for disapproval. Idaho's approach is well reasoned and therefore we continue to find that Idaho documented a reasonable approach to evaluating costs and met its obligations under 40 CFR 51.308(f)(2)(i).\", \"passage_polarity\": \"positive\", \"signals\": [{\"signal_text\": \"Idahi used a cost-effectiveness threshold that is lower than another State's threshold is not, by itself, an adequate basis for disapproval\", \"signal_type\": \"observation\", \"polarity\": \"positive\", \"rubric_matches\": [140, 141, 142]}]}]}", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 17319, "total_tokens": 17812, "completion_tokens": 493, "prompt_tokens_details": null}, "elapsed": 107.86444902420044, "agency": "EPA", "rule_title": "Air Quality State Implementation Plans; Approvals and Promulgations: Idaho; Regional Haze Plan for the Second Implementation Period", "rtc_text_len": 16505}
