{"unit_id": "FAA-2012-1058-0172", "ok": true, "issues": [], "snap_stats": {"exact": 1, "ws_normalized": 22, "no_match": 0, "anchor_only": 0, "empty": 0}, "parsed": {"unit_id": "FAA-2012-1058-0172", "passages": [{"passage_text": "Though responsive commenters provided views on \nvarious BASAs, few offered evidence of direct conflicts with the \nrequirements of those agreements. For example, BDLI commented that \ncountries with existing BASAs already contain prohibitions and \nrequirements regarding the consumption of drugs and alcohol in the \nworkplace and any violation of these prohibitions would result in \nsanctions by the aviation authority and in serious cases criminal \nprosecution but did not explicitly provide which BASAs would conflict.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "few offered evidence of direct conflicts with the \nrequirements of those agreements", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [7, 32], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}, {"signal_text": "did not explicitly provide which BASAs would conflict", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [36, 143], "_snap_kind": "exact"}], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}, {"passage_text": "As the Teamsters correctly noted, commenters have not \nidentified a specific conflict between the NPRM and the BASAs.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "As the Teamsters correctly noted, commenters have not \nidentified a specific conflict between the NPRM and the BASAs", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [7, 32, 142], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}, {"passage_text": " The FAA acknowledges the concerns raised by UK DFT and DG MOVE, \nparticularly with respect to prior notice and consultation concerning \nthe NPRM and the requirements now finalized in the rule.", "passage_polarity": "positive", "signals": [{"signal_text": " The FAA acknowledges the concerns raised by UK DFT and DG MOVE, \nparticularly with respect to prior notice and consultation concerning \nthe NPRM and the requirements now finalized in the rul", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "positive", "rubric_matches": [40, 61], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}, {"passage_text": "The final rule amends the \nproposal to address some of the concerns raised by UK DFT and DG MOVE. \nSpecifically, the FAA has revised the waiver and provided an additional \nwaiver option that gives foreign governments the ability to obtain a \nwaiver on behalf of repair stations in its territory based on \nrecognition of its program.", "passage_polarity": "positive", "signals": [{"signal_text": "The final rule amends the \nproposal to address some of the concerns raised by UK DFT and DG MOVE", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "positive", "rubric_matches": [21, 40], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}, {"signal_text": "the FAA has revised the waiver and provided an additional \nwaiver option that gives foreign governments the ability to obtain a \nwaiver on behalf of repair stations in its territory based on \nrecognition of its program", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "positive", "rubric_matches": [15, 16, 26], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}, {"passage_text": "The FAA is confident that the changes to \nthe waiver options made in response to comment will allow for a \nstreamlined process for further productive discussions and, if \nappropriate, the recognition of a country's existing requirements as a \ncompatible alternative pursuant to Sec. 120.10.", "passage_polarity": "positive", "signals": [{"signal_text": "changes to \nthe waiver options made in response to comment will allow for a \nstreamlined process for further productive discussions", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "positive", "rubric_matches": [13, 26], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}, {"signal_text": "recognition of a country's existing requirements as a \ncompatible alternative pursuant to Sec. 120.10", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "positive", "rubric_matches": [1, 15], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}, {"passage_text": "The FAA will further consult with \nparties to BASAs, where appropriate, on the impact of the final rule's \nrequirements on the relevant agreements during this three-year \nimplementation period.", "passage_polarity": "positive", "signals": [{"signal_text": "The FAA will further consult with \nparties to BASAs, where appropriate, on the impact of the final rule's \nrequirements on the relevant agreements during this three-year \nimplementation period", "signal_type": "suggestion", "polarity": "positive", "rubric_matches": [26, 78, 119], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}, {"passage_text": " The FAA disagrees with the commenters' characterization of the NPRM \nas an attempt to circumvent the requirements or purposes of the BASAs.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": " The FAA disagrees with the commenters' characterization of the NPRM \nas an attempt to circumvent the requirements or purposes of the BASA", "signal_type": "complaint", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [40, 191], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}, {"passage_text": "For these reasons, the FAA concludes that relocating the \ndrug and alcohol testing requirements applicable to part 145 repair \nstations is not appropriate or necessary.", "passage_polarity": "negative", "signals": [{"signal_text": "the FAA concludes that relocating the \ndrug and alcohol testing requirements applicable to part 145 repair \nstations is not appropriate or necessary", "signal_type": "observation", "polarity": "negative", "rubric_matches": [21, 16], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}], "_snap_kind": "ws_normalized"}, {"passage_text": "The FAA acknowledges \nthe commenters' concerns and has t